        "Name": "Mental Imagery-based Fear Extinction",
        "ReferencesAndLinks": null
      },
      "readme": "This dataset is the result of a one day study involving several phases: Habituation, Fear Conditioning Acquisition, Fear Extinction using mental imagery, Fear extinction recall using visual presentation.\n\nNote, that participants in this study did complete a previous \"Day 1\" study involving fear conditioning with different stimuli. This study was conducted outside the MRI and is described in a separate publication: Jiang, X., & Greening, S. G. (2021). Psychophysiological evidence for fear extinction learning via mental imagery. Psychophysiology, 58(11), e13906. https://doi.org/10.1111/psyp.13906\n\n\nThis dataset is made available under the Public Domain Dedication and License \nv1.0, whose full text can be found at \nhttp://www.opendatacommons.org/licenses/pddl/1.0/. \n",
